# Initial recovery slopes — source-only diagnostic candidate

This is a post-outcome software diagnostic, staged before computing its results.
It uses every one of the same eight raw initial witnesses and all360original
runs' four internal endpoint states. No PDE, new trajectory, tuning, case choice,
production import/modification or student final research design is involved.
Root must review/freeze these bytes and explicitly give GO before any arrays or
new diagnostic outcomes are computed. No result computation has occurred here.

The derivative targets are explicitly **half-relative-squared** model errors:
`.5||m-mtruth||²/||mtruth||²` and `.5||v-vtruth||²/||vtruth||²`, with `v=m^(-1/2)`.
Their directional derivatives are `(m-mtruth)·d/||mtruth||²` and
`(v-vtruth)·[-.5(v/m)d]/||vtruth||²`. Unlike relativeL2norm itself these smooth
metrics have derivativezero at exacttruth. Existing relativeL2 values remain
separate descriptives; the code does not differentiate the norm at zero.

The two directions are the actual stored unprojected proposal and exact
L2-normalized`-gtrue`, when defined. It also computes dataDDs, native-m cosines to
`mtruth-m`, and`gtrue·(mtruth-m)`. Cosine/direction undefined cases remain unknown.
No rawdirection is relabeled as a clipped optimizer displacement or finite step.
The parameter is squaredslowness in s²/km²; velocity is in km/s.

Fixed centered differences validate only the error-metric formulas on stored
arrays. The preregistered dimensionless epsilons are`1e-4` and`5e-5`; actual
`h=epsilon*min(m_i/abs(d_i))` over nonzero components guarantees positive plus/minus
models with maximumrelativecoordinate perturbation`1e-4`. No clipping/epsilon
adaptation occurs. Actualh, cancellationproxy, two-scale changes and boxviolations
are reported; neither a truncationbound nor a verifiedFPsign is claimed.
Literal derivative signs and a separate fixed numerical nearzero classification
are both retained, including adverse or unresolved cases.

All eight truth and initial models get finitepositive/minmax and literal
feasibility checks against the original`[1/36,1]` box. Exactactivebound counts,
near-FP-band flags and literal violations stay separate; nothing is clipped or
forgiven by tolerance. Every alreadyloaded endpoint also gets these counts.
Bounds misspecification must be considered before assigning causes to recovery.

Every original1/2/4/8internalstate is compared only with its owninitial. All five
arms, three repetitions, three modes and every paid/unpaid/ineligible row remain.
Original credited relativeL2 metrics are retained and checked against the raw
states. Groups are descriptive, with full and eligible denominators; there is
no between-method winner or claim that internalstates are fullyreturned results.

Positive recovery-error slopes alongside negative dataDD, or a positive dataDD
towardtruth, would supply **local numerical evidence only**. They would not prove
cycle-skipping, illposedness, nonconvexity, universal cause or an algorithm remedy.
All models are reused development geology; modes/slices/repeats are not IIDsites.
This diagnostic does not fulfill the outstanding positive matched-cost recovery,
realistic-physics, novelty or student-ownership requirements.

The protocol pins both published complete receipts, source9f, originalprotocol
and all original inputartifact hashes. Newoutput only; inputevidence untouched.
After rootreview/freeze/GO only:

```
python diagnose_initial_slopes.py --execute-reviewed-diagnostic   --repo ABSOLUTE_REPO --witness ABSOLUTE_PINNED_INITIAL_RUN   --benchmark ABSOLUTE_PINNED360RUN --output NEW_ABSOLUTE_OUTER_DIRECTORY   --expected-source-sha256 REVIEWED_SOURCE_HASH   --expected-protocol-sha256 REVIEWED_PROTOCOL_HASH
```
